{
  "id": "inlay_hints/type_hints/22_library_aliases",
  "topic": "inlay_hints",
  "subtopic": "type_hints",
  "title": "Library member aliases",
  "summary": "A member alias of a class template gives way to what it names where that reads shorter",
  "prose": "`vector<int>::size_type` shows as `size_t` and `vector<int>::reference` as `int &`, but `vector<int>::iterator` stays: what it names is the library's own. An alias a namespace declares (`int64_t`, the code's `UserId`) or a class that is no template (`steady_clock::time_point`) stays as named; one that only stands for a builtin (`duration<long>::rep`) shows the builtin.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "namespace std {\ntypedef unsigned long size_t;\ntypedef long int64_t;\n\ntemplate <class Pointer, class Container>\nstruct __normal_iterator {};\n\ntemplate <class T>\nstruct vector {\n    using reference = T&;\n    using size_type = size_t;\n    using iterator = __normal_iterator<T*, vector>;\n    reference front();\n    size_type size() const;\n    iterator begin();\n};\n\ntemplate <class Rep>\nstruct duration {\n    using rep = Rep;\n    rep count() const;\n};\n\nstruct steady_clock {\n    using time_point = int64_t;\n    static time_point now();\n};\n}  // namespace std\n\nusing UserId = std::int64_t;\nUserId current_user();\nstd::int64_t big();\n\nvoid use(std::vector<int>& values, std::duration<long> elapsed) {\n    auto count = values.size();\n    auto& first = values.front();\n    auto it = values.begin();\n    auto ticks = elapsed.count();\n    auto now = std::steady_clock::now();\n    auto user = current_user();\n    auto large = big();\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
